@prefix d4d: <https://w3id.org/bridge2ai/data-sheets-schema/> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix rai: <http://mlcommons.org/croissant/RAI/> .
@prefix evi: <https://w3id.org/EVI#> .
@prefix dcat: <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

# ==============================================================================
# D4D to RO-Crate SKOS Semantic Alignment
# ==============================================================================
# Version: 1.5
# Date: 2026-10-05
# Description: Formal semantic mappings between D4D LinkML schema and RO-Crate
#              properties using SKOS mapping predicates.
#
# Mapping Types:
#   - skos:exactMatch: Direct 1:1 mapping, no transformation needed
#   - skos:closeMatch: Semantically close, transformation required
#   - skos:relatedMatch: Related concepts, complex/partial mapping
#   - skos:broadMatch: RO-Crate term is broader than D4D term
#   - skos:narrowMatch: RO-Crate term is narrower than D4D term
# ==============================================================================

# Class-level alignments
# ==============================================================================
# The class-level rows down to CoreDistribution were reviewed 2026-09-30
# against the merged schemas' class_uri, is_a and *_mappings (#3976); the
# class-scoped rows among them are slot rows, which the comprehensive SSSOM
# generator checks against the slots' own declarations.
# Dataset is the dataset itself: the converters (src/fairscape_integration/)
# write a D4D Dataset as the RO-Crate root Dataset and read the root back as
# a Dataset, and CoreDataset, its d4d-core counterpart, declares class_uri
# dcat:Dataset and exact_mappings schema:Dataset. The full schema still declares Dataset class_uri
# dcat:Distribution and exact_mappings schema:DataDownload, a data resource
# rather than a dataset. That declaration is the one that looks wrong; it is
# recorded here for a schema change, and the exactMatch stands.
d4d:Dataset skos:exactMatch schema:Dataset .

# Added 2026-04-25 — RO-Crate root + supporting classes
# DatasetCollection: tree_root in d4d schema → projects to RO-Crate root
# (@type=["Dataset", "https://w3id.org/EVI#ROCrate"], @id="./")
# Its resources are Dataset records, which carry the exactMatch above; the
# collection projects to a Dataset entity but is not interchangeable with the
# datasets it holds (was exactMatch, #3976). The schema's exact_mappings
# dcat:Dataset belong to the model Dataset's class_uri dcat:Distribution
# comes from, in which the collection is the dataset and each Dataset a
# distribution of it.
d4d:DatasetCollection skos:closeMatch schema:Dataset .
d4d:DatasetCollection skos:closeMatch dcat:Catalog .
# File: matches schema:MediaObject in D4D_FileCollection.yaml class_uri. The
# schema also declares exact_mappings schema:DigitalDocument; two exact
# targets that are distinct schema.org types would make them one, so
# DigitalDocument stays close (#3976, kept).
d4d:File skos:exactMatch schema:MediaObject .
d4d:File skos:closeMatch schema:DigitalDocument .
# FileCollection: nested Dataset in RO-Crate hasPart. Both triples are the
# schema's own exact_mappings and close_mappings (#3976, kept).
d4d:FileCollection skos:exactMatch schema:Dataset .
d4d:FileCollection skos:closeMatch dcat:Distribution .

# Class-level slot mappings (added 2026-04-25)
d4d:DatasetCollection_resources skos:exactMatch schema:hasPart .
d4d:File_file_type skos:exactMatch d4d:fileType .
d4d:FileCollection_resources skos:exactMatch schema:hasPart .
d4d:FileCollection_collection_type skos:exactMatch d4d:collectionType .
d4d:FileCollection_file_count skos:exactMatch d4d:fileCount .
d4d:FileCollection_total_bytes skos:exactMatch dcat:byteSize .

# Added 2026-04-26 — DataSubset (full schema) + d4d-core Core* classes
# DataSubset: is_a Dataset; sub-Dataset under hasPart. A subset of a dataset
# is a narrower kind of dataset, as Grantor is of Organization (was
# exactMatch, #3976).
d4d:DataSubset skos:broadMatch schema:Dataset .
# CoreDataset (d4d-core, primary exchange-layer record). The core schema
# declares exact_mappings schema:Dataset, and dcat:Dataset as both its
# class_uri and a close mapping; the closeMatch follows close_mappings, and
# the schema's contradiction is recorded for a schema change (#3976, kept).
d4d:CoreDataset skos:exactMatch schema:Dataset .
d4d:CoreDataset skos:closeMatch dcat:Dataset .
# CoreDatasetCollection (d4d-core, RO-Crate root). The core schema declares
# class_uri and exact_mappings dcat:Catalog (was closeMatch). Its resources
# are CoreDataset records, which carry the core schema's exact_mappings to
# schema:Dataset: close, as DatasetCollection is (was exactMatch, #3976).
d4d:CoreDatasetCollection skos:closeMatch schema:Dataset .
d4d:CoreDatasetCollection skos:exactMatch dcat:Catalog .
# CoreDistribution (d4d-core, file/distribution surface). As for CoreDataset,
# the core schema declares dcat:Distribution as both its class_uri and a
# close mapping; the closeMatch follows close_mappings (#3976, kept).
d4d:CoreDistribution skos:exactMatch schema:DataDownload .
d4d:CoreDistribution skos:closeMatch dcat:Distribution .

# Added 2026-04-26 — sub-entity classes referenced via RO-Crate properties
# Reviewed 2026-09-30 (#3942). A class is aligned to the RO-Crate, schema.org
# or RAI term that carries the same entity or the same datasheet answer; a
# DatasetProperty class answering a datasheet question aligns with the
# property that carries the answer, as the schema's own class exact_mappings
# do (CleaningStrategy, ImputationProtocol, ...). Removed or corrected
# triples are recorded in comments written without their d4d:/skos: prefixes
# so neither the generators' line pattern nor a Turtle parser reads them.
d4d:Person skos:exactMatch schema:Person .
d4d:Organization skos:exactMatch schema:Organization .
# Grantor is_a Organization, so schema:Organization is the broader term (was exactMatch).
d4d:Grantor skos:broadMatch schema:Organization .
d4d:Grant skos:exactMatch schema:Grant .
d4d:VariableMetadata skos:exactMatch schema:PropertyValue .
d4d:Software skos:exactMatch schema:SoftwareApplication .
# Removed (#3942):
# - Creator exactMatch schema:Person. Creator is a team or group wrapper (a
#   principal_investigator Person, affiliations, credit_roles), not a person.
#   The alignment is carried by the creators slot (closeMatch schema:author).
# - Maintainer exactMatch schema:Person and DataCollector exactMatch
#   schema:Person. Both are role wrappers (role plus maintainer_details /
#   collector_details) whose subject may be a person or an organization; the
#   maintainers and data_collectors slots carry their alignments.
# - FundingMechanism exactMatch schema:Grant. FundingMechanism wraps a grantor
#   and its grants; Grant is the class that matches schema:Grant, and the
#   funders slot carries the alignment (exactMatch schema:funder).

# Added 2026-04-26 — DatasetProperty subclasses with natural RO-Crate / RAI analogues
# Instance describes what the instances represent (type, topic, counts,
# labels), not a measured variable: related, as the instances slot says (was closeMatch).
d4d:Instance skos:relatedMatch schema:variableMeasured .
# Removed (#3974): SamplingStrategy exactMatch evi:samplingPlan, and the
# sampling_strategies slot's relatedMatch to it. EVI 1.6, the version
# https://w3id.org/EVI resolves to (checked 2026-09-30), defines no
# samplingPlan in any serialization or its documentation page.
# LabelingStrategy bundles the annotation protocol, platform, annotations per
# item and annotator demographics; its data_annotation_protocol attribute is
# the schema's exact match for rai:dataAnnotationProtocol, so the RAI term is
# the narrower one (was exactMatch).
d4d:LabelingStrategy skos:narrowMatch rai:dataAnnotationProtocol .
d4d:InstanceAcquisition skos:closeMatch rai:dataCollection .
d4d:RawDataSource skos:exactMatch rai:dataCollectionRawData .
# RawData records whether raw data was kept and where it is; RawDataSource
# carries the schema's exact_mappings to the same term (was exactMatch).
d4d:RawData skos:closeMatch rai:dataCollectionRawData .
d4d:ImputationProtocol skos:exactMatch rai:dataImputationProtocol .
# Subpopulation describes how subpopulations are identified and distributed,
# not a measured variable: related, as the subpopulations slot says (was closeMatch).
d4d:Subpopulation skos:relatedMatch schema:variableMeasured .
d4d:CollectionTimeframe skos:exactMatch rai:dataCollectionTimeframe .
d4d:MissingDataDocumentation skos:exactMatch rai:dataCollectionMissingData .
d4d:MachineAnnotationTools skos:exactMatch rai:machineAnnotationTools .
d4d:IntendedUse skos:exactMatch rai:dataUseCases .
d4d:Purpose skos:closeMatch rai:dataUseCases .
d4d:Task skos:closeMatch rai:dataUseCases .
d4d:OtherTask skos:closeMatch rai:dataUseCases .
# ExistingUse records uses already made; IntendedUse carries the schema's
# exact_mappings to rai:dataUseCases (was exactMatch).
d4d:ExistingUse skos:closeMatch rai:dataUseCases .
d4d:DatasetBias skos:exactMatch rai:dataBiases .
d4d:DatasetLimitation skos:exactMatch rai:dataLimitations .
# VersionAccess is about support for older versions, not the version string:
# related, as the version_access slot says (was closeMatch).
d4d:VersionAccess skos:relatedMatch schema:version .
d4d:LicenseAndUseTerms skos:closeMatch schema:license .
# Confidentiality is about why data must be withheld: its examples are
# legal privilege, patient data and non-public communications. Patient
# data overlaps the personal attributes (gender, age, location ...) that
# rai:personalSensitiveInformation lists, but privilege and private
# communications do not, and the class records a confidentiality basis,
# not attribute categories. Related, not close; SensitiveElement is
# that term's exact match (was closeMatch).
d4d:Confidentiality skos:relatedMatch rai:personalSensitiveInformation .
# The schema declares SensitiveElement exact_mappings rai:personalSensitiveInformation (was closeMatch).
d4d:SensitiveElement skos:exactMatch rai:personalSensitiveInformation .
d4d:Erratum skos:closeMatch schema:correction .
d4d:UpdatePlan skos:exactMatch rai:dataReleaseMaintenancePlan .
# Limits on keeping people's data are related to, not close to, the
# conditions of access to an item (was closeMatch).
d4d:RetentionLimits skos:relatedMatch schema:conditionsOfAccess .
d4d:CollectionMechanism skos:exactMatch rai:dataCollection .
d4d:PreprocessingStrategy skos:exactMatch rai:dataPreprocessingProtocol .
d4d:CleaningStrategy skos:exactMatch rai:dataManipulationProtocol .
d4d:FutureUseImpact skos:exactMatch rai:dataSocialImpact .
# A data protection impact analysis concerns the data subjects, part of the
# social impact FutureUseImpact matches exactly (was exactMatch).
d4d:DataProtectionImpact skos:broadMatch rai:dataSocialImpact .
d4d:IPRestrictions skos:closeMatch schema:conditionsOfAccess .
d4d:DistributionFormat skos:closeMatch evi:formats .
# A distribution date is a release date, not a creation date; the class's
# release_dates attribute declares dcterms:available (was schema:dateCreated).
d4d:DistributionDate skos:closeMatch schema:datePublished .
# A repository of known uses is related to a link, as the use_repository slot says (was closeMatch).
d4d:UseRepository skos:relatedMatch schema:relatedLink .
d4d:ExternalResource skos:closeMatch schema:relatedLink .
d4d:DatasetRelationship skos:closeMatch schema:isRelatedTo .
d4d:AnnotationAnalysis skos:exactMatch rai:dataAnnotationAnalysis .
d4d:ParticipantPrivacy skos:closeMatch rai:personalSensitiveInformation .
# Splits describes recommended splits in prose; schema:hasPart links a
# dataset to its parts, which DataSubset models (was closeMatch).
d4d:Splits skos:relatedMatch schema:hasPart .
# Removed (#3942):
# - HumanSubjectResearch, InformedConsent, AtRiskPopulations, ContentWarning,
#   AddressingGap, DataAnomaly and HumanSubjectCompensation exactMatch a d4d:
#   term (humanSubject, informedConsent, atRiskPopulations, contentWarning,
#   addressingGaps, dataAnomalies, participantCompensation). A D4D target is
#   not an alignment to an external vocabulary (#3054).
# - Deidentification closeMatch rai:confidentialityLevel. confidentialityLevel
#   is an access classification, not a de-identification statement
#   (notes/D4D_GENERATION_ARMS.md, "Two left deliberately unfixed").
# - ExtensionMechanism closeMatch schema:license. A mechanism for others to
#   contribute to the dataset is not its license.
# - DiscouragedUse exactMatch rai:prohibitedUses, ProhibitedUse exactMatch
#   rai:prohibitedUses and EthicalReview exactMatch rai:ethicalReview. Neither
#   target is one of the 20 properties Croissant RAI 1.0 defines (the
#   reference table in data/schema_comparison/schemas/croissant_rai/, and the
#   RAI fields of fairscape_models' Croissant model), and schema.org defines
#   neither prohibitedUses nor ethicalReview, the unprefixed names FAIRSCAPE
#   crates emit (notes/D4D_GENERATION_ARMS.md). A discouraged use is also not
#   a prohibited one: ProhibitedUse is "stronger than DiscouragedUse".
# - Relationships closeMatch schema:isRelatedTo. Relationships documents links
#   between instances inside the data (ratings, social links), not between
#   datasets; DatasetRelationship is the class for the latter.

# Added 2026-04-26 — final gap-fill (consent workflow + access control)
d4d:DirectCollection skos:closeMatch rai:dataCollection .
d4d:ExportControlRegulatoryRestrictions skos:closeMatch schema:conditionsOfAccess .
d4d:MissingInfo skos:closeMatch rai:dataCollectionMissingData .
d4d:ThirdPartySharing skos:closeMatch schema:conditionsOfAccess .
d4d:FormatDialect skos:closeMatch schema:encodingFormat .
# Removed (#3942): CollectionConsent, CollectionNotification and
# ConsentRevocation closeMatch rai:personalSensitiveInformation. Consent,
# notice and revocation are not sensitive personal attributes, and no
# offline vocabulary here names a consent term.

# Direct/Exact Mappings (45 triples)
# ==============================================================================
# These properties map directly without transformation

d4d:title skos:exactMatch schema:name .
d4d:description skos:exactMatch schema:description .
d4d:doi skos:exactMatch schema:identifier .
d4d:keywords skos:exactMatch schema:keywords .
d4d:language skos:exactMatch schema:inLanguage .
d4d:license skos:exactMatch schema:license .
d4d:publisher skos:exactMatch schema:publisher .
d4d:version skos:exactMatch schema:version .
d4d:page skos:exactMatch schema:url .
d4d:download_url skos:exactMatch schema:contentUrl .
d4d:bytes skos:exactMatch schema:contentSize .
d4d:md5 skos:exactMatch evi:md5 .
d4d:sha256 skos:exactMatch evi:sha256 .
d4d:hash skos:exactMatch evi:md5 .
d4d:created_on skos:exactMatch schema:dateCreated .
d4d:issued skos:exactMatch schema:datePublished .
d4d:last_updated_on skos:exactMatch schema:dateModified .
d4d:status skos:exactMatch schema:creativeWorkStatus .
d4d:conforms_to skos:exactMatch schema:conformsTo .
d4d:was_derived_from skos:exactMatch schema:isBasedOn .

# Removed (#3971, #4052): the slot-level twins of the seven classes #3942
# found aligned to a d4d: term (see "Removed (#3942)" above), as their class
# triples were. Each slot holds that class's objects, and each said
# exactMatch to the same D4D term: addressing_gaps addressingGaps, anomalies
# dataAnomalies, content_warnings contentWarning, informed_consent
# informedConsent, human_subject_research humanSubject, at_risk_populations
# atRiskPopulations and participant_compensation participantCompensation. A
# D4D target is not an alignment to an external vocabulary (#3054), for a
# slot as for its class. Four of the seven restated the slot's own slot_uri.
# The other three are keys the FAIRSCAPE converters write
# (src/fairscape_integration/); no slot_uri, class_uri or element name in
# the schema is one of them (the slot_uris are anomalies, contentWarnings and
# humanSubjectResearch).

# RAI namespace - exact matches
d4d:collection_mechanisms skos:exactMatch rai:dataCollection .
d4d:collection_timeframes skos:exactMatch rai:dataCollectionTimeframe .
d4d:future_use_impacts skos:exactMatch rai:dataSocialImpact .
# Settled 2026-09-30 (#3971, #3995, #4002) and 2026-10-01 (#4052): each slot-level twin of a
# class triple #3942 corrected or removed now carries what its class
# carries, as the slot holds that class's objects; where the class triple
# was removed, the twin's is removed too. That includes the nine twins no
# TODO marked: labeling_strategies, raw_sources and the seven twins of the
# classes aligned to d4d: terms (removed above). Twins whose predicate
# changed moved to the section their predicate names (confidential_elements,
# data_protection_impacts, distribution_dates, existing_uses,
# labeling_strategies, raw_sources, retention_limit, sensitive_elements).
# Removed (#3971): discouraged_uses and prohibited_uses exactMatch
# rai:prohibitedUses, and ethical_reviews exactMatch rai:ethicalReview, as
# the DiscouragedUse, ProhibitedUse and EthicalReview class triples were.
# Neither target is one of the 20 Croissant RAI 1.0 properties (the reference
# in data/schema_comparison/schemas/croissant_rai/; the published RAI
# specification names neither, checked 2026-09-30), and schema.org defines
# neither prohibitedUses nor ethicalReview, the unprefixed keys FAIRSCAPE
# crates emit. A discouraged use is also not a prohibited one.

# Settled 2026-10-05 (#4036): ten slot-level triples disagreed in strength
# with the class-level triple of the class the slot holds (its range), on
# the same target. Nine now carry their class's predicate, each for the
# reason in the comment above it, taken from the target's definition and
# the slot's and the class's descriptions in the merged schema. Four whose
# class the schema maps exactly (exact_mappings) moved here from "Close
# Matches" (annotation_analyses, cleaning_strategies,
# machine_annotation_tools, preprocessing_strategies); five whose class is
# close moved there (acquisition_methods, errata, related_datasets, tasks,
# other_tasks). The tenth, distribution_formats, is left as found (see
# "FAIRSCAPE Evidence namespace" below). A test checks the rule for every
# slot whose range is a class with a class-level triple, and lists that one
# exception with its reason
# (tests/test_semantic_exchange/test_skos_alignment_header.py).

# Intended uses. rai:dataUseCases is "Intended applications and usage
# guidelines" (the repository's Croissant RAI 1.0 list,
# data/schema_comparison/schemas/croissant_rai/). intended_uses holds
# IntendedUse objects, "explicit intended and recommended uses", and the
# schema maps IntendedUse exactly to this term (exact_mappings), so the slot
# and the class carry the one exact match to it. tasks and other_tasks said
# exactMatch too, and exactMatch is transitive, so the three slots were one
# concept although the schema asks three questions. They are close now, as
# their classes are (see "Close Matches"), and so are purposes and
# existing_uses (#4036).
d4d:intended_uses skos:exactMatch rai:dataUseCases .
d4d:purposes skos:closeMatch rai:dataUseCases .
d4d:known_biases skos:exactMatch rai:dataBiases .
d4d:known_limitations skos:exactMatch rai:dataLimitations .
# rai:dataImputationProtocol, as the ImputationProtocol class, its schema
# exact_mappings and fairscape_models name it (#3926; was rai:imputationProtocol).
d4d:imputation_protocols skos:exactMatch rai:dataImputationProtocol .
d4d:missing_data_documentation skos:exactMatch rai:dataCollectionMissingData .
d4d:raw_data_sources skos:exactMatch rai:dataCollectionRawData .
# The slot holds SensitiveElement objects, which the schema maps exactly to
# this term (exact_mappings), and fairscape_models fills sensitive_elements
# from it: exact, as the class is (was closeMatch, #4002).
d4d:sensitive_elements skos:exactMatch rai:personalSensitiveInformation .
d4d:updates skos:exactMatch rai:dataReleaseMaintenancePlan .

# Annotation analyses, machine annotation tools, cleaning and
# preprocessing. Each slot holds objects of a class the schema maps exactly
# to the term (exact_mappings), and the slot's description names what the
# term names (the repository's Croissant RAI 1.0 list):
# - annotation_analyses (AnnotationAnalysis): "analyses of annotation
#   quality and inter-annotator agreement"; the term, "Analysis of
#   annotation quality and agreement".
# - machine_annotation_tools (MachineAnnotationTools): "automated annotation
#   tools used in dataset creation"; the term, "Automated annotation tools
#   and models".
# - cleaning_strategies (CleaningStrategy): "data cleaning and quality
#   control procedures"; the term, "Data cleaning and transformation
#   procedures". The schema puts transformation steps under
#   preprocessing_strategies, so the two vocabularies divide this work
#   differently; the class's exact_mappings is what makes this exact.
# - preprocessing_strategies (PreprocessingStrategy): "preprocessing steps
#   applied to the raw data", normalization and transformation among them;
#   the term, "Preparation steps for ML processing".
# Exact, as each class is (was closeMatch, #4036). They sat under a heading
# that read close as a string-to-object transformation, but every
# slot-level rai: triple in this file is on a slot that holds class
# objects, the exact matches above included, so that does not separate
# close from exact.
d4d:annotation_analyses skos:exactMatch rai:dataAnnotationAnalysis .
d4d:cleaning_strategies skos:exactMatch rai:dataManipulationProtocol .
d4d:machine_annotation_tools skos:exactMatch rai:machineAnnotationTools .
d4d:preprocessing_strategies skos:exactMatch rai:dataPreprocessingProtocol .

# FAIRSCAPE Evidence namespace - exact matches
# distribution_formats is left as found (#4036): it says exactMatch where
# the DistributionFormat class it holds says closeMatch. EVI 1.6 defines no
# formats term (#4037), so no definition settles either strength, and #4037
# decides every triple on evi:formats. Until then the test of the
# slot/class strength rule lists this disagreement as an exception, with
# that reason.
d4d:distribution_formats skos:exactMatch evi:formats .
d4d:encoding skos:closeMatch evi:formats .
d4d:funders skos:exactMatch schema:funder .

# Metadata and structure
d4d:citation skos:exactMatch schema:citation .
d4d:format skos:exactMatch schema:encodingFormat .
d4d:parent_datasets skos:exactMatch schema:isPartOf .
d4d:same_as skos:exactMatch schema:sameAs .
d4d:variables skos:exactMatch schema:variableMeasured .

# JSON-LD identifier
d4d:id skos:exactMatch rdf:ID .

# Close Matches (20 triples)
# ==============================================================================
# Semantically close but require transformation

# String to Person/Organization object
d4d:creators skos:closeMatch schema:author .
d4d:created_by skos:closeMatch schema:creator .
d4d:modified_by skos:closeMatch schema:contributor .

# Uses already made. rai:dataUseCases names recommended uses and usage
# guidelines; uses the dataset has already served are close to that, not the
# same: close, as the ExistingUse class is (was exactMatch, #4002).
d4d:existing_uses skos:closeMatch rai:dataUseCases .

# Release dates. A distribution date is a release date, not a creation date
# (the class's release_dates attribute declares dcterms:available), and may
# be a planned date or a timeframe: close to schema:datePublished, as the
# DistributionDate class is (was exactMatch schema:dateCreated, #3971).
d4d:distribution_dates skos:closeMatch schema:datePublished .

# Raw data kept. The slot holds RawData objects, which record whether raw
# data was kept and where it is; raw_data_sources (RawDataSource, the
# schema's exact_mappings) carries the exact match: close, as the RawData
# class is (was exactMatch, #3971).
d4d:raw_sources skos:closeMatch rai:dataCollectionRawData .

# Tasks. tasks holds Task objects, "Tasks the dataset is intended to
# support" (specific machine learning, research or analytical tasks), and
# other_tasks holds OtherTask objects, "Additional tasks the dataset may
# support beyond its original intent". Both name applications of the
# dataset, which rai:dataUseCases ("Intended applications and usage
# guidelines") covers; but intended_uses carries the exact match to that
# term, and three exact matches made three questions one concept. Close, as
# the Task and OtherTask classes are (both were exactMatch, #4036).
d4d:tasks skos:closeMatch rai:dataUseCases .
d4d:other_tasks skos:closeMatch rai:dataUseCases .

# Instance acquisition. The slot holds InstanceAcquisition objects, which
# say how the data for each instance was acquired: directly observed,
# reported by subjects, inferred or derived, validated. rai:dataCollection
# is the "Description of the data collection process", and
# collection_mechanisms carries the exact match to it, as the
# CollectionMechanism class it holds does (exact_mappings): "What mechanisms
# or procedures were used to collect the data". How each instance's data
# was acquired answers another question about collection, and two exact
# matches made the two one concept. Close, as the InstanceAcquisition class
# is (was exactMatch, #4036).
d4d:acquisition_methods skos:closeMatch rai:dataCollection .

# Errata. The slot holds Erratum objects: "Known errors or corrections to
# the dataset since publication", each with a link to the erratum
# (erratum_url) and a description of "the error, its scope, the affected
# data or records, and the correction applied" (erratum_details).
# schema:correction "Indicates a correction to a CreativeWork" (schema.org,
# as rdflib ships it). A known error that has no correction yet is not one.
# Close, as the Erratum class is (was exactMatch, #4036).
d4d:errata skos:closeMatch schema:correction .

# Related datasets. The slot holds DatasetRelationship objects, each a typed
# relationship (relationship_type: supplements, derives from, is version
# of) to another dataset (target_dataset). schema:isRelatedTo is "A pointer
# to another, somehow related product (or multiple products)" (schema.org,
# as rdflib ships it): untyped, and between products. Close, as the
# DatasetRelationship class is (was exactMatch, #4036). The schema
# serialises the slot as this term (slot_uri), so the comprehensive
# generator lists the slot as an accepted disagreement of strength only.
d4d:related_datasets skos:closeMatch schema:isRelatedTo .

# Multiple properties to single field
d4d:license_and_use_terms skos:closeMatch schema:license .
d4d:ip_restrictions skos:closeMatch schema:conditionsOfAccess .
# Removed (#3971): extension_mechanism closeMatch schema:license, as the
# ExtensionMechanism class triple was. A way for others to extend or
# contribute to the dataset (contribution_url, extension_details) is not its
# license.
d4d:regulatory_restrictions skos:closeMatch schema:conditionsOfAccess .

# Format/dialect transformations
d4d:compression skos:closeMatch evi:formats .
d4d:dialect skos:closeMatch schema:encodingFormat .
d4d:media_type skos:closeMatch schema:encodingFormat .

# Privacy and ethical considerations
d4d:participant_privacy skos:closeMatch rai:personalSensitiveInformation .

# Subject categorization
d4d:themes skos:closeMatch schema:about .

# External resource relationship
d4d:external_resources skos:closeMatch schema:relatedLink .

# Related Matches (10 triples)
# ==============================================================================
# Related concepts requiring complex or partial mapping

# Complex structured data
d4d:instances skos:relatedMatch schema:variableMeasured .
d4d:subpopulations skos:relatedMatch schema:variableMeasured .

# Confidential data. Confidentiality records why data must be withheld (legal
# privilege, patient data, non-public communications); only patient data
# overlaps the personal attributes this term lists, and SensitiveElement and
# sensitive_elements carry the exact match to it: related, as the
# Confidentiality class is (was exactMatch, #3995).
d4d:confidential_elements skos:relatedMatch rai:personalSensitiveInformation .

# Retention limits. Limits on keeping people's data are related to the
# conditions of access to an item, neither narrower nor broader: related, as
# the RetentionLimits class is (was narrowMatch, which made the target the
# narrower term although the comment above it said the opposite, #3971).
d4d:retention_limit skos:relatedMatch schema:conditionsOfAccess .

# Collection structures
d4d:resources skos:relatedMatch schema:hasPart .

# Data collectors with compensation details
d4d:data_collectors skos:relatedMatch schema:contributor .

# Maintainers (not directly in RO-Crate)
d4d:maintainers skos:relatedMatch schema:maintainer .

# Subset information
d4d:subsets skos:relatedMatch schema:hasPart .
# Removed (#3974): sampling_strategies relatedMatch evi:samplingPlan; EVI
# defines no samplingPlan (see the SamplingStrategy note above).

# Versioning and access
d4d:version_access skos:relatedMatch schema:version .

# Repository tracking
d4d:use_repository skos:relatedMatch schema:relatedLink .

# Narrow/Broad Matches (6 triples)
# ==============================================================================
# Where scope differs between D4D and RO-Crate

# D4D path is more specific than generic RO-Crate file path
d4d:path skos:narrowMatch schema:contentUrl .

# Removed (#3971): is_deidentified narrowMatch rai:confidentialityLevel, as the
# Deidentification class triple was. confidentialityLevel is not a Croissant
# RAI 1.0 property, and in FAIRSCAPE crates it holds an access classification,
# not a de-identification statement (notes/D4D_GENERATION_ARMS.md).

# D4D tabular flag is narrower than general format
d4d:is_tabular skos:narrowMatch schema:encodingFormat .

# Data protection impact. An analysis of the impact on data subjects is part
# of the social impact future_use_impacts matches exactly: broad, as the
# DataProtectionImpact class is (was exactMatch, #4002).
d4d:data_protection_impacts skos:broadMatch rai:dataSocialImpact .

# Labeling strategies. The slot holds LabelingStrategy objects, which bundle
# the annotation protocol with its platform, annotations per item and
# annotator demographics; their data_annotation_protocol attribute is the
# schema's exact match for this term: narrow, as the LabelingStrategy class
# is (was closeMatch, #3971).
d4d:labeling_strategies skos:narrowMatch rai:dataAnnotationProtocol .

# D4D schema/class conformance is narrower than general conformsTo
d4d:conforms_to_class skos:narrowMatch schema:conformsTo .
d4d:conforms_to_schema skos:narrowMatch schema:conformsTo .

